e,"url":"https://tandridge.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-03","committee":"Audit & Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://tandridge.moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-06-25","committee":"Full Council","time":"8.30 pm","status":"Confirmed; Extraordinary Meeting","webcast":false,"url":"https://tandridge.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-16","committee":"Full Council","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://tandridge.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-28","committee":"Audit & Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://tandridge.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Planning Policy Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://tandridge.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Strategy & Resources Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://tandridge.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Homelessness and temporary accommodation costs are highly volatile and present a material downside risk to budget","lead":"Temporary accommodation is a high-volatility cost line and the council's own commentary shows it lacks full control over the exposure; significant growth could force reserve drawdowns or service cuts.","iso":"2026-09-10","paper_title":"Appendix A Month 3 Q1 2026-27 Budget Monitoring - Housing Services Committee","paper_url":"https://tandridge.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s19924/19924.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Housing improvements delayed into 2027 due to resource constraints and contractor procurement issues","lead":"Capital delivery delays directly affect the council's ability to execute its housing strategy and may indicate capacity or financing constraints that extend beyond this year.","iso":"2026-09-10","paper_title":"Appendix A Month 3 Q1 2026-27 Budget Monitoring - Housing Services Committee","paper_url":"https://tandridge.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s19924/19924.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Six council house building schemes paused, creating \u00a37.5m capital slippage against \u00a334.4m HRA capital budget","lead":"A lender needs to understand whether housing delivery capacity and financing arrangements are intact; paused schemes across six separate locations suggests systemic issues, not temporary timing slips.","iso":"2026-09-10","paper_title":"Appendix A Month 3 Q1 2026-27 Budget Monitoring - Housing Services Committee","paper_url":"https://tandridge.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s19924/19924.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-10","committee":"Housing Committee","paper_title":"Appendix A Month 3 Q1 2026-27 Budget Monitoring - Housing Services Committee","paper_url":"https://tandridge.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s19924/19924.pdf","headline":"Homelessness and temporary accommodation costs are highly volatile and present a material downside risk to budget","detail":"The report explicitly flags that temporary accommodation costs are \"very sensitive to changes\" and that \"a small increase in numbers can have a significant impact on the budget\". A reserve exists to mitigate Housing Benefit impacts, but the underlying exposure is uncontrolled. Current spend is tracking as expected, but the sensitivity is high.","category":"demand","matters":"Temporary accommodation is a high-volatility cost line and the council's own commentary shows it lacks full control over the exposure; significant growth could force reserve drawdowns or service cuts.","figures":"Sensitivity flagged but no current variance disclosed; reserve exists to mitigate impact on Housing Benefit","quote":"Spend to-date is in line with expectations, but a small increase in numbers can have a significant impact on the budget. Temporary Accommodation costs can also have a knock-on impact on Housing Benefit (although a reserve exists to mitigate the impact on the latter).","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-10","committee":"Housing Committee","paper_title":"Appendix A Month 3 Q1 2026-27 Budget Monitoring - Housing Services Committee","paper_url":"https://tandridge.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s19924/19924.pdf","headline":"Housing improvements delayed into 2027 due to resource constraints and contractor procurement issues","detail":"Door and window replacement, thermal insulation and communal works slipped \u00a31,274k as new contractors are \"unlikely to be in place before December\". Warm Homes Wave 3 delayed \u00a3605k due to resource and planning constraints. Stock condition survey is now being outsourced to a contractor because in-house capacity cannot complete it.","category":"capital","matters":"Capital delivery delays directly affect the council's ability to execute its housing strategy and may indicate capacity or financing constraints that extend beyond this year.","figures":"\u00a31,274k Door and Window / Thermal Insulation slippage; \u00a3605k Warm Homes Wave 3 slippage; \u00a355k additional contractor costs for Stock Condition Survey","quote":"(\u00a31,274k) Door and Window Replacement, Thermal Insulation ,Communal works and Garages and Outhouses mainly slipped due to resource/procurement issues and new contractors unlikely to be in place before December.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-10","committee":"Housing Committee","paper_title":"Appendix A Month 3 Q1 2026-27 Budget Monitoring - Housing Services Committee","paper_url":"https://tandridge.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s19924/19924.pdf","headline":"Six council house building schemes paused, creating \u00a37.5m capital slippage against \u00a334.4m HRA capital budget","detail":"Schemes at Warren Lane, Stanstead Road, Stychens Lane, Kentwyns, Hurst Green Methodist Church and Dormers are paused and contributing the majority of the \u00a312.3m underspend in Council House Building. This represents a 40% variance on the HRA capital programme and indicates material delays to the housing development pipeline.","category":"capital","matters":"A lender needs to understand whether housing delivery capacity and financing arrangements are intact; paused schemes across six separate locations suggests systemic issues, not temporary timing slips.","figures":"\u00a37,494k net slippage on paused schemes; \u00a312,263k total Council House Building underspend out of \u00a334,444k total HRA capital available","quote":"(\u00a37,494k) net slippage - (\u00a37,021k) of the slippage relates to paused schemes at Warren Lane, Stanstead Road Stychens Lane, Kentwyns, Hurst Green Methodist Church and Dormers.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-10","committee":"Housing Committee","paper_title":"Quarter 1 202627 Budget Monitoring - Housing Committee","paper_url":"https://tandridge.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s19923/19923.pdf","headline":"Homelessness and housing benefit costs flagged as ongoing budget risks for General Fund","detail":"The Housing General Fund is currently forecasting a \u00a35k full-year overspend at Q1. The Council specifically notes that risks around homelessness and housing benefit costs are 'being monitored, managed and may present as a variance later in the financial year', indicating these are cost pressures with uncertain outturn.","category":"demand","matters":"A lender will be alert to whether homelessness and housing benefit pressures force a General Fund variance that the council cannot absorb within the \u00a3750k GF housing budget. These are both demand-driven costs sensitive to economic conditions and cannot easily be controlled.","figures":"Housing General Fund budget \u00a3750k; Q1 forecast overspend \u00a35k; homelessness and housing benefit flagged as monitored risks","quote":"Risks to the General Fund budget around Homelessness and the cost of Housing Benefit are being monitored, managed and may present as a variance later in the financial year.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-10","committee":"Housing Committee","paper_title":"Quarter 1 202627 Budget Monitoring - Housing Committee","paper_url":"https://tandridge.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s19923/19923.pdf","headline":"HRA capital programme shows \u00a314,133k slippage (41% of total budget not expected to be spent)","detail":"The HRA capital budget was set at \u00a334,444k (including carry-forwards) but the Council is forecasting spend of only \u00a320,311k, representing net underspends and slippage of \u00a314,133k. This is nearly two-fifths of the capital budget. The cause of this substantial slippage is not explained in the report.","category":"capital","matters":"A lender needs to assess the council's capital delivery capability. Slippage this large\u2014particularly when under-spending is recorded in Q1 of the financial year\u2014suggests either project delays, delivery constraints, or scope changes that will affect the housing improvement programme.","figures":"\u00a334,444k budget; \u00a320,311k forecast; \u00a314,133k slippage","quote":"For the Housing Revenue Account, a budget including carry-forwards and adjustments of \u00a334,444k is available, as set out in paragraphs 7-9. The current forecast is \u00a320,311k with net underspends and slippage of (\u00a314,133k).","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-10"},"name":"Tandridge","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-26","since_iso":"2026-08-27","distress":false,"headline":"Homelessness and temporary accommodation costs are highly volatile and present a material downside risk to budget","lead":"Temporary accommodation is a high-volatility cost line and the council's own commentary shows it lacks full control over the exposure; significant growth could force reserve drawdowns or service cuts.","also":["6 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Audit & Scrutiny Committee on 2026-09-29","n_findings":7,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Appendix A Month 3 Q1 2026-27 Budget Monitoring - Housing Services Committee","top_paper_url":"https://tandridge.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s19924/19924.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":89,"news_drafts_total":3}}